ndencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in Godot v4.5.beta4.mono\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta4.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nE 0:00:04:613   _build_step_find_edge_connection_pairs: Navigation map synchronization error. Attempted to merge a navigation mesh polygon edge with another already-merged edge. This is usually caused by crossing edges, overlapping polygons, or a mismatch of the NavigationMesh / NavigationPolygon baked 'cell_size' and navigation map 'cell_size'. If you're certain none of above is the case, change 'navigation/2d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale' to 0.001.\n  <C++ Source>  modules/navigation_2d/2d/nav_map_builder_2d.cpp:140 @ _build_step_find_edge_connection_pairs()\n\n<img width=\"945\" height=\"229\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33abafd7-a423-47ac-ad78-57778e5ad3b7\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHave a big tileset with a lot of tiles, select all the tiles in the TileSet and assign the navigation to the entire Tile, as shown below:\n\n<img width=\"758\" height=\"521\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a0bfd45-ae2c-4689-af09-17faa73a18bd\" />\n\n<img width=\"328\" height=\"620\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/492be6fd-cb5d-429a-b236-724d8806d465\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nJust create a TileMapLayer and TileSet with the steps mentioned.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Re